+**Liberty:** the 1871 context's existing sparse reconstructed planting now draws through the shared adaptive seasonal tree renderer instead of its portable kit's rounded solid crowns. The proxy uses the grown open deciduous habit also used by the street elms, bounded by each context record's nominal height and crown width. It does not identify any context tree as an elm. Its positions, reconstructed grades, source limits and inspection identities remain those of L-1871-city-baseline. Spring, summer and fall use that renderer's corresponding leaf cover, and winter uses bare wood. The shared Trees setting and confidence hide apply to the handed-off records. No context planting is moved or removed by this renderer change.
